{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>And when it lengthened.</b> And if it [the cloud] lingered — this is the general rule — and afterward he says: whether it was two days or a month or longer, they would encamp. But the wording here is by way of generality, and afterward he says: by the word of YHWH they would journey, and by the word of YHWH they would encamp. Or: and if it lingered — this is by way of generality, and afterward he says: by the word of YHWH they would journey or encamp."], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:16:56.823331004Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}